//font-weight: bold

// The type treatment of a Monaco line number: face, size, weight, and the
// sub-pixel nudge that settles it on the line box.
//
// APPEARANCE ONLY, and shared for that reason — the unified diff calls it too
// (components/unified_diff.styl), so the two editors cannot drift into
// different-looking gutters again.  What is deliberately NOT here is layout:
// the width of the lane and what the number aligns against differ by editor,
// and it was exactly a layout property leaking across that stretched the
// diff's labels over its `+`/`-` markers.
line-number-type()
  font-family: "SpaceMono"
  font-weight: 300
  line-height: inherit
  font-size: 0.875rem !important
  padding-top: 0.0625em !important

// The line the cursor is on.
//
// Monaco marks it with `.active-line-number`, and both gutters already change
// COLOUR for it rather than opacity — #858585 to #C6C6C6.  Two problems with
// that: neither value is one of ours (they are Monaco's built-in vs-dark
// defaults, see the note in ui/editor.nim's theme file), and both were then
// halved by the resting `opacity: 0.5`, so the active number landed at an
// effective rgb(119,119,119) — barely a step up from its neighbours.
//
// Here it is a design token at full strength: `text/primary/label`, the role
// the UI uses for a label that is currently the subject.  The dimming is lifted
// for this one row, which is what makes it read as selected at all.
//
// Applies to both gutters, so it is deliberately NOT inside the `:not()` below:
// the editor nests its number one level deeper, in `.gutter-line`, so that box
// has to be undimmed too or the wrapper's full opacity is undone by the child.
.line-numbers.active-line-number
  color: colors-ui-text-primary-label !important
  opacity: 1

  .gutter-line
    color: colors-ui-text-primary-label !important
    opacity: 1

// Scoped away from the unified diff on purpose.
//
// `width: 100% !important` beats the `width` Monaco writes inline, which is how
// every other editor here gets its line numbers pushed right, up against the
// code.  That works where the gutter holds nothing else.
//
// The unified diff's gutter does hold something else: Monaco splits it into a
// line-number lane and a decorations lane (the `+` / `-` markers in
// components/unified_diff.styl), and `100%` is the width of BOTH.  Stretching
// the label across the pair right-aligned it to the code edge, which left the
// slack on the left of the gutter and covered the markers completely — they
// were rendering, with `.line-numbers` painted over them.
//
// There is no way to give Monaco's inline width back from another rule, so the
// fix is for this one not to match.
.line-numbers:not(.unified-diff-editor *)
  // border-right: 0.0625em solid colors-ui-border-primary
  line-number-type()
  width: 100% !important
  display: block !important
  box-sizing: border-box
  margin-left: 0 !important
  text-align: right !important
  margin-top: 0em !important
  padding-right: 0 !important
  // color: LINE_NUMBERS_TEXT_COLOR !important

